      "note": "Cross-cutting observation: The project maintains a clean zero-Critical/High security posture across all security-audited WPs. The primary systemic risk is the fire-and-forget logging pattern — ErrorLogManager.append() is synchronous but exceptions at disk level propagate unhandled at multiple call sites (Router, three orchestrators). A lightweight stderr fallback should be added as a project-wide convention before this tool expands to more integration points. Additionally, two incomplete logging surface areas remain from the original plan: (1) git-status.ts .catch(()=>undefined) is still silent, (2) storage I/O layer has no error-log injection — both are natural next-session targets."
    }
